s come to pay tribute, and inhabited by merchants from various countries.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-5-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1005014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3ed22fed6b604b18aba1de519bfcfbbb0dbfc509fe67e8029dc14ac301388766","compact":"7cec6c48c87d1dc0230749bcd05f43a427a82bbaab49b954f1bf1316cccabc63","nasal":"d3e5c25ac9ad1a257da119f04a7200421e386ea3aaf5de82aad4b8dd494b87c9"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-5-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":5,"verse":15,"english":"And adorned with mountain like palaces glittering with gems, and filled with sportingplaces for females, and like to Indra's Amarāvati.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.706,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-5-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1005015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1a7c9afe4598181b45a4b6ba4c26e95572c37d0f5e5c9e24544e1d8849ebf8cc","compact":"98eba9a5610909aa8a98e6e04742350d026245401c978ce8599ed5ae1dee225c","nasal":"d2ac014f089683465f5d76075620c603f1f29595302597633adabd31c2aa1083"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-5-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":5,"verse":16,"english":"The city was wonderful to behold, gleaming with gold-burnished ornaments, and inhabited by troops of courtezans, and abounding in all kinds of gems, and graced with royal palaces.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-5-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1005016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b323e44fa4c5a7ffc9d14c869c99a1020f208923f14a3c98b78726dd641a911e","compact":"cf804afd5fab83080d5bcbfad22ee1bebb4e37c407e6d3194d84854486b5fc37","nasal":"cf804afd5fab83080d5bcbfad22ee1bebb4e37c407e6d3194d84854486b